summary.text:
LEN not available? Odd. Maybe need to avoid LEN; use string indexing until NUL, bounded by upper bound. I could use a WHILE loop scanning for 0 terminator. Let me rewrite without LEN.

Use i := 1; WHILE i <= 254 DO read c; if c = 0 exit.

Also string indexing needs proper access. ipText[i] works in CODESYS? Yes, STRING index access returns BYTE in CODESYS 3.5. Let me implement state machine with WHILE loop.

Careful: handle empty string, trailing dot.

Implementation:

ipValue := 0;
seg := 0;
val := 0;
digits := 0;
ok := TRUE;
i := 1;
WHILE (i <= 254) AND ok DO
  c := ipText[i];
  IF c = 0 THEN EXIT; END_IF
  ... as before but can't EXIT inside with ok set? Use ok:=FALSE then EXIT.
END_WHILE

Then IF ok AND (digits>0) AND (seg=3) THEN pack final else 0.

Actually careful: EXIT from loop on NUL is fine.

Note: after loop, if ok and seg=3 and digits>0 -> add val.

Also need to avoid overflow on val with huge digits: val UDINT *10 could overflow. "999999999999999999999.2.3.4" — val overflow wraps but we break as soon as val>255, at the 4th digit max. Since we check val>255 right after adding, at most val ~2559 before break. Fine.

Let me write it.

